<title>USA: TENNIS-LIPTON CHAMPIONSHIPS RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-LIPTON CHAMPIONSHIPS RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>KEY BISCYANE, Florida 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results at the</p>
<p>$4.45 million Lipton Championships tennis tournament on Friday</p>
<p>(prefix number denotes seeding):</p>
<p>Men's singles, first round</p>
<p>Chris Woodruff (U.S.) beat Alex Radulescu (Germany) 6-4 6-4</p>
<p>Julian Alonso (Spain) beat Steve Bryan (U.S.) 6-4 6-0</p>
<p>Daniel Nestor (Canada) beat Jonathan Stark (U.S.) 6-3 0-6 6-3</p>
<p>Jeff Tarango (U.S.) beat Sargis Sargsian (Armenia) 6-2 7-5</p>
<p>Nicklas Kulti (Sweden) beat Marcos Ondruska (South Africa)</p>
<p>6-0 6-2</p>
<p>Jeff Salzenstein (U.S.) beat Johan Van Herck (Belgium) 6-7</p>
<p>(5-7) 6-3 6-4</p>
<p>Jerome Golmard (France) beat Guillaume Raoux (France) 6-2 6-3</p>
<p>Sebastien Lareau (Canada) beat Mark Woodforde (Australia) 6-2</p>
<p>6-4</p>
<p>Gaston Etlis (Argentina) beat Galo Blanco (Spain) 6-4 6-4</p>
<p>Magnus Larsson (Sweden) beat Paul Haarhuis (Netherlands) 7-5</p>
<p>0-6 7-5</p>
<p>Slava Dosedel (Czech Republic) beat Doug Flach (U.S.) 7-6</p>
<p>(7-1) 2-6 6-2</p>
<p>Dominik Hrbaty (Slovakia) beat Thierry Champion (France) 6-7</p>
<p>(3-7) 7-5 6-3</p>
<p>Scott Draper (Australia) beat Sjeng Schalken (Netherlands)</p>
<p>6-3 7-6 (7-5)</p>
<p>Women's singles, second round</p>
<p>1-Martina Hingis (Switzerland) beat Patricia Hy Boulais</p>
<p>(Canada) 3-6 6-3 6-2</p>
<p>Tommy Haas (Germany) beat Guy Forget (France) 7-6 (7-3) 7-5</p>
<p>Sandon Stolle (Australia) beat Marcos Aurelio Gorriz (Spain)</p>
<p>6-0 6-7 (0-7) 7-5</p>
<p>Grant Stafford (South Africa) beat Leander Paes (India) 7-6</p>
<p>(7-4) 7-6 (7-5)</p>
<p>Men's singles, second round</p>
<p>4-Goran Ivanisevic (Croatia) beat Byron Black (Zimbabwe) 6-3</p>
<p>6-3</p>
<p>9-Wayne Ferreira (South Africa) beat Jiri Novak (Czech</p>
<p>Republic) 6-4 6-2</p>
<p>Mark Philippoussis (Australia) beat Martin Damm (Czech</p>
<p>Republic) 7-5 7-6 (7-4)</p>
<p>Women's singles, second round</p>
<p>4-Monica Seles (U.S.) beat Naoko Sawamatsu (Japan) 6-3 2-6</p>
<p>6-2</p>
<p>10-Mary Joe Fernandez (U.S.) beat Annabel Ellwood (Australia)</p>
<p>6-4 6-4</p>
<p>Magdalena Maleeva (Bulgaria) beat Lindsay Lee (U.S.) 6-3 6-3</p>
</text>
